    "title": "Introduction: White Blood Cells and Immune Defence",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">White blood cells are specialised cells in the blood that defend the human body against pathogens such as bacteria and viruses. They do this by producing <strong>antibodies</strong> that target and destroy the invading pathogens, and <strong>antitoxins</strong> that neutralise harmful toxins released by pathogens.</p>",
