    "title": "How Vaccination Works",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Vaccination works by deliberately introducing small quantities of dead or inactive forms of a pathogen into the body. This stimulates white blood cells to produce antibodies without causing the full disease. This prepares the immune system to fight future infections by the same pathogen.</p>",
